## Why This Is Asked

This question probes designing a latency-sensitive, privacy-respecting, explainable inference service with multi-tenant isolation in AWS, plus lifecycle and cost awareness.

## Key Concepts

- PrivateLink, VPC, Private Data Lake, per-tenant isolation
- SageMaker endpoints, Feature Store, Model Registry
- Real-time explainability paths (Clarify/SHAP) with low latency
- Canary rollout, drift detection, monitoring and cost

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: route to appropriate prod/canary endpoint
function route(tenantId){
  const inCanary = ['tenantA','tenantB'];
  const ep = inCanary.includes(tenantId) ? 'fraud-prod-canary' : 'fraud-prod';
  return ep;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce strict per-tenant data access controls across services?
- How would you validate explainability fidelity at high throughput?
- How would you handle retraining triggers when drift is detected per tenant?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience building production ML pipelines in AWS with strict data locality, latency targets, and privacy. Assesses ability to combine PrivateLink, Lake Formation, Feature Store, canary deployment, drift monitoring, and cost governance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker PrivateLink
- Lake Formation data access
- Feature Store
- Endpoint traffic splitting (canary)
- Drift detection & retraining triggers
- DP privacy controls and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example drift score calculation (KS statistic placeholder)
function ksDrift(p, q) {
  let max = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < p.length; i++) {
    max = Math.max(max, Math.abs(p[i] - q[i]));
  }
  return max;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rollback if canary drift triggers fire?
- What metrics and thresholds would you alert on for latency, FP rate, and drift?
